1
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:25,640
YAMU!

2
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:28,377
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:29,800
YAMU!

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,620
Your moves!

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,420
It's time to duel!

6
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:11,980
All over the island, my
unwitting pawns are in place.

7
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:18,140
The duels have begun, and by now, the slow
process of elimination is well underway.

8
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:21,937
Only the strongest duel
monsters players will survive,

9
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:25,373
and those of insufficient
skill will fall by the wayside.

10
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:27,400
Okay, bring them on.

11
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:31,057
I'm itching to duel, and I'm
taking on the next player we see.

12
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:33,820
You know, I'm not so
sure Joey's up to this.

13
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:36,117
Yeah, there are
tournament-level players here,

14
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:38,737
but don't you think he's
smart enough to realize?

15
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:41,526
Here I stand, the next
Duel Monsters Champion!

16
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:44,800
He needs a reality check.

17
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:47,295
Guess he's about as smart as he looks.

18
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:49,388
I'd better be the champion.

19
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,580
For Serenity's sake.

20
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:55,960
She's always counted on
me, even when we were kids.

21
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:03,660
Where are we, Joey?

22
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:06,457
Where have you taken
me today, big brother?

23
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:07,580
To the beach.

24
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:09,722
That's what you said you wanted.

25
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:15,320
Hey, Joey. Yeah?

26
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:18,360
You're the world's best brother.

27
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:26,780
Oh, Joey.

28
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:29,300
It looks so pretty.

29
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,220
And so cold!

30
00:02:42,420 --> 00:02:43,860
What a great day!

31
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,492
We gotta come back here!

32
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:47,040
But how?

33
00:02:47,820 --> 00:02:48,650
Don't worry.

34
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:51,557
Even if Mom and Dad do get
divorced and we have to live apart,

35
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:54,464
I'll still bring you back
to this place someday.

36
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:55,520
You promise?

37
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:58,600
Yeah, I promise.

38
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:02,444
I'm your big brother, Serenity.

39
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:04,017
I'm supposed to take care of you.

40
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:06,457
I'm going to win this
tournament and the prize money.

41
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:08,357
I'm going to make sure you
don't lose your eyesight

42
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:11,277
and show you that beautiful
ocean one more time.

43
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:12,440
I promise.

44
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:16,580
Look there.

45
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:19,940
Duel Monster Stadiums.

46
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,100
Look at them.

47
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:23,360
They're all over.

48
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:27,000
You said it.

49
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:29,017
Lots of dueling going on. Right.

50
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:31,377
I'm going in you sure you want to do this

51
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:33,477
if you lose you give
up your only star chip.

52
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:34,390
That's right

53
00:03:36,020 --> 00:03:39,920
Don't panic you can do this
Joey you do know that don't you?

54
00:03:40,260 --> 00:03:43,077
I hope you're right Yugi this
will be my first official

55
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:46,457
duel and I can't afford to get
knocked out at the start True,

56
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:48,364
but not everyone here is a pro.

57
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:50,957
I'm sure you can find
someone on your level go

58
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:54,017
for someone easy Joey And
I guess I should think

59
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:56,097
about what kind of field
my cards are best suited

60
00:03:56,180 --> 00:03:58,827
for they're mostly
monsters and fighter types

61
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:02,600
Uh, I guess that makes this
meadow region my kind of turf.

62
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:03,677
That's right, Joey.

63
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:04,590
See?

64
00:04:04,673 --> 00:04:05,503
You know what you're doing.

65
00:04:05,586 --> 00:04:07,200
You lost, Crybaby.

66
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:08,967
Now give me your star chips.

67
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:11,737
A voice that annoying
can only belong to...

68
00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:12,857
my...

69
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:13,777
It's not fair.

70
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:15,017
You cheated somehow.

71
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:17,877
How could you know what your cards
were when they were still face down?

72
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:20,740
I'm psychic, and you're done.

73
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:28,437
Well, look who's here.

74
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:31,140
Wow, Mai's already won
two more Star Chips.

75
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:32,650
Hmm.

76
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:36,040
Hey, Yugi, are your duels going well?

77
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:37,456
I'm making progress.

78
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:39,880
So you have three Star Chips, do you?

79
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:42,880
I might be up for a duel myself. Take her.

80
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:45,737
Knock her out of the
contest and off the island.

81
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:50,080
Hmm, you know, I'm definitely in
the mood for a duel right now.

82
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:54,700
So get ready, because I
choose to challenge you, Joey.

83
00:04:55,220 --> 00:04:56,050
What?

84
00:04:56,133 --> 00:04:56,963
You challenge me?

85
00:04:57,046 --> 00:04:58,940
Do you have the guts to accept?

86
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:01,610
Get it?

87
00:05:01,693 --> 00:05:02,872
I want to play you, kid.

88
00:05:03,780 --> 00:05:04,610
Huh.

89
00:05:04,693 --> 00:05:05,697
Guess you heard about my skill.

90
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:07,133
Don't flatter yourself.

91
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:09,977
I overheard you and Yugi
talking on the boat,

92
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:12,957
and I know he gave you the
only star chip that you have.

93
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:16,220
My motto is, take out the
weakest players first.

94
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:17,957
And considering that you wouldn't even be

95
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:20,077
here if Yugi hadn't given
you one of his chips,

96
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:22,457
you've got to be the weakest
duelist on the island.

97
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:25,437
Hey, do you have to be so... insulting?

98
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:29,260
This time she was being
truthful. Huh? Mai's ruthless.

99
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:30,577
Don't duel her first.

100
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:31,490
Don't you get it?

101
00:05:31,573 --> 00:05:34,226
If you lose this contest,
you're out for good.

102
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:36,180
Yugi, stand up for Joey.

103
00:05:36,380 --> 00:05:38,439
You have to fight her in his place.

104
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:42,640
This is his decision to make.

105
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:44,797
Show Mai what you're made of.

106
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:45,710
Right.

107
00:05:45,793 --> 00:05:48,280
She thinks I'm a pushover,
but she'll see. Yugi!

108
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:49,997
You can't be serious, Joey.

109
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:52,740
I've never been more
serious. Don't you see?

110
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,840
This is my chance to prove myself.

111
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:56,820
To show everybody.

112
00:05:57,760 --> 00:05:59,700
Don't forget, Gramps trained me.

113
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:01,330
I mean,

114
00:06:01,413 --> 00:06:03,777
sure, Gramps didn't get a
chance to finish my training,

115
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:04,690
and granted,

116
00:06:04,773 --> 00:06:06,897
I wish I'd had a chance to
practice more before getting

117
00:06:06,980 --> 00:06:09,877
thrown into a tournament this
huge with so many heavy hitters,

118
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:10,790
but honest,

119
00:06:10,873 --> 00:06:11,703
I think I can take her.

120
00:06:11,786 --> 00:06:12,616
Oh, man.

121
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:13,920
You better be right.

122
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:15,620
For your sister's sake.

123
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:18,512
Yeah, you better not screw this up, Joey.

124
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:20,200
I accept. Let's duel.

125
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,840
Get ready to lose.

126
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:27,380
Go get her, Joey!

127
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,540
Kick her butt! Yeah!

128
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:32,380
He'll do fine.

129
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,880
Since you only have one measly star chip,

130
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:38,649
I only have to bet one
of mine against you.

131
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:42,219
At least this region will
give me a field advantage.

132
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:43,510
Huh?

133
00:06:43,593 --> 00:06:44,423
Oh, no!

134
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:47,357
What are all those
mountains doing on my field?

135
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:50,040
The field we'll battle on is 40 % forest,

136
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:52,917
40 % mountain, and the
last 20 % is meadow.

137
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,240
So deal with it or surrender.

138
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:57,540
Calm down, Joey. You'll be okay.

139
00:06:57,980 --> 00:07:01,917
Your monsters will still get a field power
bonus on the meadow part of the field.

140
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:02,840
Oh, yeah.

141
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:08,297
Listen, Mai, not for nothing, but I gotta
ask you one question before we duel.

142
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:09,240
Hmm? What?

143
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:12,237
Why did you decide to take
part in this tournament?

144
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:15,060
Tell me, Mai, why is it you duel?

145
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:16,640
Why do I duel?

146
00:07:16,860 --> 00:07:18,297
For all the comforts that I crave.

147
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:21,317
Designer clothes, travel, perks,
anything to avoid real work.

148
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:24,200
Hot cars, turbocharged for living large.

149
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:26,557
So that's why you want the prize money?

150
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:27,470
How selfish.

151
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:29,157
How dare you try and judge me?

152
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:31,537
Who do you think you are,
you pathetic little snot?

153
00:07:31,620 --> 00:07:33,740
Hey, you're only dueling for things.

154
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:37,937
But for your information, some of
us fight for the people we love.

155
00:07:38,020 --> 00:07:39,057
You'll show her, Joey.

156
00:07:39,140 --> 00:07:41,317
Show her what it's like
to duel from the heart.

157
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:42,230
Duel.

158
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:47,920
So to start the game off,
Masaki, the legendary swordsman.

159
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:54,460
Ooh, the field power bonus will
bring his power up over 300 points.

160
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:57,220
Hey, I made my first move. Hmm.

161
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:00,270
Huh?

162
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:01,990
Hmm?

163
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:05,484
What do you think you're doing?

164
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:07,040
Divining my card.

165
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:11,000
I have to mystically choose which
one of them's the best. Huh?

166
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:12,920
What are you, a psychic?

167
00:08:13,440 --> 00:08:15,460
And the best card would be...

168
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:19,820
The Harpy's Lady.

169
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:27,540
Her strength is boosted by the
mountain's field power bonus.

170
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:30,040
I'll still take it on.

171
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:35,020
Joey, wait!

172
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:38,535
Land monsters are at a
disadvantage to flying monsters.

173
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:44,397
Monsters that can fly
have a magical resistance

174
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:46,997
against monsters that can
only walk on the earth.

175
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:49,080
So Joey blew it already? No,

176
00:08:49,220 --> 00:08:53,985
but he attacked too soon before he thought
about what her monster was capable of.

177
00:08:55,460 --> 00:08:57,100
My samurai sushi!

178
00:08:57,640 --> 00:09:00,420
Oh, card, speak to me!

179
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:06,800
And I'll choose again
without looking. Huh?

180
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:08,200
How's she doing that?

181
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:09,640
He's losing it.

182
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:12,585
Guess that mop head wasn't
ready for this duel.

183
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:16,466
Hey, Joey, think about what you're
doing before you move again.

184
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:20,074
How can she read the cards
when they're lying face down?

185
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:22,377
My little card trick
has made this kid forget

186
00:09:22,460 --> 00:09:25,048
everything he ever knew
about duel monsters.

187
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:29,940
All I have to do is just keep
pushing his buttons. What do I do?

188
00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:32,040
Maybe eat this one.

189
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,480
Tiger Axe!

190
00:09:34,220 --> 00:09:37,017
My field power bonus should
raise its attack power,

191
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:39,924
so it can take on the
Harpies Lady head to head.

192
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:41,597
You're not thinking.

193
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:43,317
It's still resistant to magic.

194
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:44,230
Right.

195
00:09:44,313 --> 00:09:47,258
Tiger Axe is another
handicapped Earth-based monster.

196
00:09:54,020 --> 00:09:58,726
It'll take stronger monsters than your
land-based wimps to beat my Harpy's Lady.

197
00:09:58,940 --> 00:10:01,877
Now I'll play this lovely
card without even looking.

198
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,195
I'll give you a hint.

199
00:10:03,340 --> 00:10:07,517
It's an equipment magic card that will
help me defeat your next card in one turn.

200
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:09,659
Again, with all that psychic stuff?

201
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:11,620
Can she see my cards, too?

202
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,517
Since I can't see what she's
playing, I gotta get defensive.

203
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:17,040
Running scared, huh?

204
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:19,740
Well, let me show you my surprise.

205
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:22,820
Cyber Shield to juice up my Harpy's Lady.

206
00:10:32,740 --> 00:10:33,570
No!

207
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:36,300
How's she doing that?

208
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:38,940
This is so much fun!

209
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:42,617
In case you were wondering, the next card
you were thinking of won't work either.

210
00:10:42,700 --> 00:10:44,620
Mai has ESP. It has to be it.

211
00:10:44,760 --> 00:10:48,701
I'm going to lose this duel match
and the chance to save my sister.

212
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:59,620
This game is mine.

213
00:10:59,860 --> 00:11:02,140
You can't win against me. She's right.

214
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,517
She's too much for me.

215
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:04,430
Settle down.

216
00:11:04,513 --> 00:11:08,397
Joey, remember what my grandpa taught
you about how to play duel monsters.

217
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:09,951
Don't let her rattle you.

218
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:12,139
She's just trying to psych you out.

219
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:15,260
Stay out of this. Huh?

220
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:17,677
Your brainless cheerleading
isn't going to help

221
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:20,697
him against the superior
power of my harpy ladies.

222
00:11:20,780 --> 00:11:22,320
Don't you guys get it yet?

223
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:25,077
Friendship doesn't win duels, never will.

224
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:26,017
It hasn't helped him.

225
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:28,620
He's defeated and he knows it. Not true.

226
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:30,697
No, I beg to differ.

227
00:11:30,780 --> 00:11:32,780
There can be only one champion.

228
00:11:33,180 --> 00:11:34,797
On this island, in this game,

229
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:38,880
someone can be your best friend
today and your worst enemy tomorrow.

230
00:11:39,160 --> 00:11:42,577
Once the competition forces you
to face each other in a duel,

231
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:44,640
where's your friendship then?

232
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:48,332
That's why the only person a
duelist can trust is himself.

233
00:11:48,620 --> 00:11:52,091
I hope that your defeat today
teaches you that lesson, kid.

234
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:54,880
He's losing it!

235
00:11:54,980 --> 00:11:55,940
He needs help!

236
00:11:56,060 --> 00:11:57,120
Yugi, help him!

237
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:01,220
Yu-Gi-Oh!

238
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,417
Don't listen to her, Joey.

239
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:17,957
We're here to help you, just
like you're always there for us.

240
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:19,360
Huh? What?

241
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:20,720
Trust me on this.

242
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:25,477
She's just trying to divide and conquer a
strategy that's been used for centuries.

243
00:12:25,560 --> 00:12:26,720
Believe me, I know.

244
00:12:26,900 --> 00:12:30,724
When you get that look in your
eye, I believe everything you say.

245
00:12:31,580 --> 00:12:34,897
Do you really think Yugi wants
you to be the grand prize winner?

246
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:36,497
He's a duelist, too, you know.

247
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:38,457
To win, you'll eventually
have to take him on.

248
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:39,370
She's right.

249
00:12:39,453 --> 00:12:40,475
We will have to duel.

250
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:41,590
But...

251
00:12:42,580 --> 00:12:44,917
Yugi, you're the best friend I ever had.

252
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:45,830
Don't worry.

253
00:12:45,913 --> 00:12:47,117
We'll rescue your grandfather.

254
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:48,257
We'll do it together.

255
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:49,240
We're a team.

256
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:51,400
We are a team.

257
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:54,424
But I also have to win
the contest for Serenity.

258
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:59,357
I'm sending you this video just so you
don't forget your little sister's face.

259
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:01,680
It seems like I'm running out of time.

260
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:02,841
Take care, Joey.

261
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:04,910
What do I do?

262
00:13:04,993 --> 00:13:07,038
Maybe Yuki's right about this thing.

263
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:11,380
I have to stop listening to Mai's
nonsense and start using my head.

264
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:15,704
I just gotta concentrate
on how to win the game.

265
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:22,917
There's gotta be a way to beat Mai.

266
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:26,237
If I can just figure out how
she knows what her cards are,

267
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:30,026
if she's not psychic, there must
be something else she's doing.

268
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:33,700
What's that strange smell?

269
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:38,077
I never noticed that smell
when my eyes were open.

270
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:43,140
I'm smelling a bunch of different
perfumes coming from her cards.

271
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:45,157
Let's go, kid.

272
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:47,320
It's your turn. That's it.

273
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:50,340
I see through your card trick. Huh?

274
00:13:50,920 --> 00:13:54,380
You sprayed all your cards
with different perfumes.

275
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:58,036
And by smelling each different scent,

276
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:01,497
you can tell which card is which
even when they're face down.

277
00:14:01,580 --> 00:14:04,756
So you don't have to look
in order to play your cards.

278
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:07,137
That way you can psych
the other player out.

279
00:14:07,220 --> 00:14:08,050
No way!

280
00:14:08,133 --> 00:14:11,317
How could an amateur punk like
you see through my aroma strategy?

281
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:12,635
It's just impossible!

282
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:17,277
I gotta admit, Mai, you really had me
buying into the whole psychic powers shtick.

283
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:20,877
I was too freaked out to think
things through because of that.

284
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:22,842
But you're not a psychic at all.

285
00:14:23,060 --> 00:14:24,620
You're just a big fake.

286
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:25,861
All right, Joey.

287
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:27,920
Go get her, Joey. You the man.

288
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:29,540
Yuki, you were right.

289
00:14:29,820 --> 00:14:33,157
Just because you saw through
my little psychic act doesn't

290
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:36,077
mean you're going to be
able to defeat me in a duel.

291
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:37,395
I think you're wrong.

292
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:40,877
Before, you were winning by confusing me
and trying to pit me against my friends.

293
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:42,097
But now my mind is clear.

294
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:43,640
I know who I can trust.

295
00:14:43,860 --> 00:14:48,331
All you've got left is your cheap tricks,
and I won't fall for them anymore.

296
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:51,900
I'm gonna blast your harpies
out of the sky with this.

297
00:14:52,060 --> 00:14:53,060
Good card, Joey.

298
00:14:53,260 --> 00:14:54,180
Baby dragon.

299
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:01,840
That wimpy card is your grand play?

300
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:04,937
I only wish it was worth some
more so when I devastate you,

301
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:07,257
it would do more damage
to your life points.

302
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:10,460
My card will be Elegant Egotist.

303
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:14,020
Its magic will make duplicates
of my harpies, lady.

304
00:15:17,040 --> 00:15:17,870
Oh, no!

305
00:15:18,620 --> 00:15:19,450
Harpies, lady.

306
00:15:19,533 --> 00:15:21,860
One, two, three.

307
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:25,980
It's three times the trouble. Now what?

308
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:28,197
He was struggling when there was only one.

309
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:29,456
Don't give in, Joey.

310
00:15:29,540 --> 00:15:31,517
You've still got all kinds of moves left.

311
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:32,430
Really?

312
00:15:32,513 --> 00:15:33,343
What moves would those be?

313
00:15:33,426 --> 00:15:34,256
How would I know?

314
00:15:34,339 --> 00:15:35,940
Ask an expert. Ask Yugi.

315
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:37,260
It's Joey's duel.

316
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:38,892
He has to figure it out.

317
00:15:39,580 --> 00:15:42,697
I don't have any cards strong
enough to beat three harpy ladies.

318
00:15:42,780 --> 00:15:43,610
Ha!

319
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:46,277
And I'm going to keep
using the magic of elegant

320
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:50,120
egotists to double my harpies
again and again each turn.

321
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:55,400
But while my harpies multiply, I
can't attack you, so it's your move.

322
00:15:55,860 --> 00:15:58,277
Of course, you'll soon
be up against an army.

323
00:15:58,360 --> 00:15:59,760
An army of harpies?

324
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,802
How the heck do I fight an army?

325
00:16:08,660 --> 00:16:10,037
She's got a whole army.

326
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:11,897
How am I supposed to beat that?

327
00:16:11,980 --> 00:16:14,620
Don't give up, Joey. Huh?

328
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:17,105
Think hard about her strategy.

329
00:16:17,220 --> 00:16:19,337
She's been using only one monster card and

330
00:16:19,420 --> 00:16:22,361
strengthening that one
card with many magic cards.

331
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:25,853
But there's a serious flaw in
her dueling strategy, Joey.

332
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:28,540
Using magic on one card? That's true.

333
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:31,297
She's just been juicing up
the harpy ladies every turn.

334
00:16:31,380 --> 00:16:35,257
But if she has mostly magic cards, maybe
the harpy ladies are her only monsters.

335
00:16:35,340 --> 00:16:39,037
I bet if I can just defeat her harpy,
she won't have any monsters left to play.

336
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,077
That's right, Joey.

337
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:43,820
Now think, what card in
your deck will help you win?

338
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:46,340
Which of my cards? You tell me.

339
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:49,160
Wait, I think maybe you did.

340
00:16:50,180 --> 00:16:52,180
Salamandra and a kunai with chain?

341
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:55,520
Baby dragon and shield and sword? Great!

342
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:59,057
With these new magic cards
combined with your monsters,

343
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:00,737
you'll have a real strong deck.

344
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:01,650
Alright!

345
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:04,580
Here, add this to your deck.

346
00:17:04,860 --> 00:17:06,860
It can be helpful in a tight spot.

347
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:08,960
The Time Wizard.

348
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:12,717
This is the kind of tight spot
Yugi must have been talking about.

349
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:16,977
Now, if I can just remember what Gramps
taught me about the way to use a magic card,

350
00:17:17,060 --> 00:17:18,217
it's my only chance.

351
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:20,000
But do I have it in my hand?

352
00:17:20,140 --> 00:17:22,837
If I had known how long it was
going to take you to make a move,

353
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:24,537
I would have brought a magazine.

354
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:25,450
Uh-oh.

355
00:17:25,533 --> 00:17:27,221
The time wizard's not in my hand.

356
00:17:27,820 --> 00:17:29,291
I'll have to draw for it.

357
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:32,068
But what if I don't get it?

358
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:34,070
What if...

359
00:17:34,153 --> 00:17:35,457
Trust in your cards, Joey.

360
00:17:35,540 --> 00:17:36,599
Trust in yourself.

361
00:17:37,700 --> 00:17:38,560
Here I go.

362
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:40,136
It's all or nothing.

363
00:17:44,660 --> 00:17:45,780
All right!

364
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:47,215
It's the Time Wizard!

365
00:17:51,220 --> 00:17:52,660
What good is that thing?

366
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:54,020
Don't you know?

367
00:17:54,260 --> 00:17:56,620
The Time Wizard can make time go faster,

368
00:17:56,760 --> 00:18:01,280
causing my baby dragon to grow into
a thousand dragon. Right, Joey.

369
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:04,717
And that's not the only effect
your Time Wizard will have.

370
00:18:04,800 --> 00:18:05,700
Time Wizard!

371
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:15,660
Baby dragon, transform
into a thousand dragons!

372
00:18:18,540 --> 00:18:21,560
So now you have a bigger dragon. Big deal.

373
00:18:21,840 --> 00:18:24,277
My harpy ladies still
have greater attack power.

374
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:26,580
Attack it, my three harpy sisters!

375
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:29,230
What?

376
00:18:29,313 --> 00:18:31,077
What happened to my harpy ladies?

377
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:32,454
They've gotten so old!

378
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:35,600
I warned you.

379
00:18:35,820 --> 00:18:37,897
A millennium has passed
on the playing field and

380
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:40,745
your harpy ladies have
become old and decrepit.

381
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:44,460
Face it, Mai, time's running
out for you and your ladies.

382
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:50,520
I believed, and the cards
came through for me. Awesome!

383
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:52,700
Go, Thousand Dragon!

384
00:18:56,620 --> 00:18:58,880
Attack with Inferno! Flame Brad!

385
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:10,940
He did it! Joey won!

386
00:19:11,580 --> 00:19:12,797
I knew you could do it.

387
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:13,800
Thanks, guys.

388
00:19:15,960 --> 00:19:16,790
How?

389
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:20,060
How could I ever lose to such an amateur?

390
00:19:20,540 --> 00:19:22,120
Hey, Mai. Huh?

391
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:23,697
I tried to tell you,

392
00:19:23,780 --> 00:19:27,437
there's more to duel monsters than
just kicking the other guy's butt.

393
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:29,777
If you're ever going
to be a real champion,

394
00:19:29,860 --> 00:19:32,257
you've got to learn to care about someone.

395
00:19:32,340 --> 00:19:33,516
Other than yourself.

396
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:35,233
Isn't that right, Yugi?

397
00:19:35,660 --> 00:19:36,490
Mm-hmm.

398
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:40,313
I'm proud of you, Joey.

399
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:43,312
All your hard work and training paid off.

400
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:46,377
You went from a guy with nothing
but eagerness and attitude

401
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:50,720
to a winning duelist who battles
with his head and his heart.

402
00:19:58,720 --> 00:19:59,550
Yo!
